  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3206.02 Inspection Area Requirements",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3206.02 Inspection Area Requirements.\n\n(a) Each inspection station shall:\n\n(1) Have a testing space that has no obstructions and is large enough for a mechanic to walk around a vehicle with its doors open;\n\n(2) Be a minimum of 12 feet by 25 feet in length, if the station inspects motor vehicles;\n\n(3) Be a minimum of 12 feet by 50 feet in length, if the station is equipped with a headlight testing screen or board; and\n\n(4) Be a minimum of 8 feet by 12 feet in length, if the station inspects only motorcycles, and have a compliant sound inspection area per Saf-C 3236.03.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
